    -ssh : enables SSH authentication for headless clients
 
+   -tailscale : enable Tailscale-based authentication. For each incoming connection the
+                server shells out to "tailscale whois --json <client-ip>"; if that call
+                returns a Tailscale user the client is logged in as that user with no
+                credential prompt (the GitHub handle is used as the Ghidra username, e.g.
+                Tailscale LoginName "alice@github" -> "alice"; other providers use the
+                local part of the LoginName). If the CLI call fails (non-Tailscale client,
+                daemon not running, etc.) the connection falls through to the regular
+                -a# authentication flow. Users must already exist in the server, or
+                -autoProvision must be set. The "tailscale" executable must be on PATH,
+                or its path may be overridden via -Dghidra.server.tailscale.cli=<path>.
+
    <repository_path> : Required.  Directory used to store repositories. This directory must be dedicated to this 
                        Ghidra Server instance and may not contain files or folders not produced
                        by the Ghidra Server or its administrative scripts.
